 "headline": "Two pre-registered experiments, same 4 arms, 20 claims each, equal model and budget. Experiment 1 (plans from memory): centralized swarm 19, decentralized 18 (1 fabricated id), isolated 17, single agent 13; replicate ordering identical. Experiment 2 (web fetch required, hard cap): centralized 18, decentralized 17, isolated 16, single 12, zero fabricated ids everywhere, ordering as predicted beforehand. The centralized swarm beats the single agent and the isolated workers in both; the single agent costs about a tenth as much. Three findings drafted as Project Delphi nanopubs (unsigned, unpublished; np check passes) in swarm/nanopubs/.",
